(3493863, 480541, 60862, '<td valign="top">Hey, this rocks!  Very creative and I like the angle. :)<br/> <br/>I think your score suffered for the slight blurring and how her hair disappears into the background.<br/> <br/>On your camera (mine, too), try this:  hold up your hand where you expect your eyes to be, press the shutter halfway, then press the manual focus lock.  Then set the timer to take 10 shots.  It''s very hard to get your face in exactly the right position, esp. that close up, where slight changes make large focus differences.  But taking 10 shots gives you a better chance of nailing one of them.<br/> <br/>I regularly take multiple shots like this.<br/> <br/>Also, since you seem to be holding something interesting, I''d suggest using a smaller aperture (larger f-number) and getting that in focus, too.</td>', 'Hey, this rocks!  Very creative and I like the angle. :) I think your score suffered for the slight blurring and how her hair disappears into the background. On your camera (mine, too), try this:  hold up your hand where you expect your eyes to be, press the shutter halfway, then press the manual focus lock.  Then set the timer to take 10 shots.  It''s very hard to get your face in exactly the right position, esp. that close up, where slight changes make large focus differences.  But taking 10 shots gives you a better chance of nailing one of them. I regularly take multiple shots like this. Also, since you seem to be holding something interesting, I''d suggest using a smaller aperture (larger f-number) and getting that in focus, too.', '2007-03-28 11:52:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(3494166, 477945, 60862, '<td valign="top">Fantastic use of light!</td>', 'Fantastic use of light!', '2007-03-28 14:00:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3496139, 479680, 70689, '<td valign="top">This pic deserved its low grade. It''s slightly ou-of-focus, but with this kind of DOF, that''s quite a big deal. I didn''t notice the red boat in the back while taking the photo, and what''s worse, I didn''t think of cropping the picture to get ridd of it. All in all, IQ is below my own standards, I shouldn''t have submitted it.<br/> <br/>Please note that it''s made with the 50mm 1.8, not the 35mm 2.0<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-03-30 06:07:05.</i></td>', 'This pic deserved its low grade. It''s slightly ou-of-focus, but with this kind of DOF, that''s quite a big deal. I didn''t notice the red boat in the back while taking the photo, and what''s worse, I didn''t think of cropping the picture to get ridd of it. All in all, IQ is below my own standards, I shouldn''t have submitted it. Please note that it''s made with the 50mm 1.8, not the 35mm 2.0', '2007-03-29 04:38:14.000000', '2007-03-30 07:07:05.000000', 0),
